  "title": "Week 25: AI Locally on Browser",
  "date": "2025-06-12T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 25: AI Locally on Browser\n\nThis week I focused on two main things: Langchain 🧠 and Hugging Face transformer.js 🛠️.\nI learnt how a multi-modal agent works 🎯 and how to run models directly in the browser 🌐.\n\nA model can be quite big—anywhere from 10 MB to 2 GB 📦—so downloading it in a webpage isn’t very user-friendly.\nThe Background Fetch API ⏳ is a good solution, but it’s only supported in Chrome and Edge.\nI think providing a download link ⬇️ for users to fetch the model themselves, and then verifying the file’s hash 🔍, is also a good complement.\n\n🧩 bitECS\n\nNext week, I’ll try making something using Babylon.js Editor 🎮 and bitECS ⚡.",
